      "writtenOn": "2022-07-27T16:50:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll address this comment, but I had a question while I have you here: do you prefer this to be user-configurable or can I go ahead and simply enable it? I\u0027m mostly concerned about side-effects of trivial_abi for non-Chromium users of Skia. The most prominent side-effect is that sk_sp arguments to functions will be destroyed in callee\u0027s stack frame rather than caller\u0027s stack frame which can lead to undefined behavior with poorly written code - see go/unique-ptr-trivial-abi for examples from google3. Chromium is generally immune to such issues because Windows C++ ABI also destroys in callee.",
      "parentUuid": "dd176ca6_8288ecda",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 215,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "7b65454bf6f5b2bbc32912e534ba9fcb034e76be",
